/.idea
.venv/
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/worktrees/
.claude/cache/
# Secrets: MUST live here, not in .git/info/exclude — that file is not versioned,
# so a fresh clone / second machine / contributor would get the repo unprotected
# (#387). `.env` carries CREDENTIALS (service-account JSON with private_key),
# API keys and a site password; `secret.key` is a stale local copy of the Fernet
# key that used to decrypt the session file (#386 removed both the file and the
# code that wrote the key — the ignore stays so an old working copy cannot commit
# it now).
.env
.env.*
# ...but a values-free template MUST stay committable: without this negation
# `.env.*` would silently swallow it, and the omission would only surface as a
# contributor wondering which variables exist.
!.env.example
secret.key
# A Telethon session authenticates a *user* account — full read of every private
# chat plus sending as the owner. Encrypting it does not make it publishable:
# `anon.session.encrypted` sat in this public repo for two years, and rotating the
# key cannot un-publish a blob that forks already hold (#386). Both forms are
# ignored by pattern, so a differently-named session file cannot slip through.
*.session
*.session.encrypted
__pycache__/
.coverage
.audit-tmp/
.mypy_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
pytest-cache-files-*/
htmlcov/
# editable-install / build artifacts (pip install -e .)
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
